WEBVTT

00:00:04.938 --> 00:00:07.133
We, the people of Earth,

00:00:07.207 --> 00:00:10.472
greet you in a spirit
of peace and humility.

00:00:10.543 --> 00:00:12.807
As we venture out
of our solar system,

00:00:12.879 --> 00:00:16.440
we hope to earn the trust
and friendship of other worlds.

00:00:20.620 --> 00:00:22.212
Can you reduce the interference?

00:00:22.288 --> 00:00:23.380
I'm trying.

00:00:25.158 --> 00:00:27.149
What is it?

00:00:27.227 --> 00:00:28.785
I don't know.

00:00:28.862 --> 00:00:30.887
Distance?

00:00:33.666 --> 00:00:36.635
It just entered the atmosphere.

00:02:36.923 --> 00:02:39.824
They evolved from dinosaurs?

00:02:39.893 --> 00:02:41.724
Hadrosaurs, to be precise.

00:02:41.794 --> 00:02:44.490
Their ancestors settled
in the Delta Quadrant

00:02:44.564 --> 00:02:45.826
20 million years ago.

00:02:45.899 --> 00:02:48.129
The Voth, the Kobali,
the Vaadwaur.

00:02:48.201 --> 00:02:50.692
You've made first contact
with more species

00:02:50.770 --> 00:02:52.738
than any captain
since James Kirk.

00:02:52.805 --> 00:02:54.796
It helps being
the only Starfleet ship

00:02:54.874 --> 00:02:56.307
within 30,000 light-years.

00:02:56.376 --> 00:02:58.469
You are being too humble.

00:02:58.545 --> 00:03:00.979
From the first time you spoke up
in my classroom,

00:03:01.047 --> 00:03:02.480
I knew you'd go far.

00:03:02.549 --> 00:03:05.484
A little farther
than I expected, Professor.

00:03:05.552 --> 00:03:08.350
I have my Admiral hat
on today, Kathryn,

00:03:08.421 --> 00:03:10.855
and I didn't call
just to catch up.

00:03:10.924 --> 00:03:13.256
Starfleet has a mission for you.

00:03:13.326 --> 00:03:15.726
We, the people of Earth

00:03:15.795 --> 00:03:19.060
greet you in a spirit
of peace and humility.

00:03:19.132 --> 00:03:21.157
As we venture out
of our solar system,

00:03:21.234 --> 00:03:25.170
we hope to earn the trust
and friendship of other worlds.

00:03:26.206 --> 00:03:27.468
Friendship I.

00:03:27.540 --> 00:03:30.134
I had to memorize
that recording in third grade.

00:03:30.210 --> 00:03:31.472
Me, too.

00:03:31.544 --> 00:03:34.240
I even built a model
of the probe.

00:03:34.314 --> 00:03:36.839
Then this should look familiar.

00:03:43.056 --> 00:03:45.115
It was launched in 2067.

00:03:45.191 --> 00:03:47.523
Just four years
after Zefram Cochrane

00:03:47.594 --> 00:03:49.425
tested his first warp engine.

00:03:49.495 --> 00:03:51.190
What was it designed to do?

00:03:51.264 --> 00:03:52.959
Reach out to other species.

00:03:53.032 --> 00:03:54.693
Pave the way for all
the manned missions

00:03:54.767 --> 00:03:55.791
that would follow.

00:03:55.868 --> 00:03:57.426
They packed it
with information...

00:03:57.503 --> 00:03:59.095
translation matrices,

00:03:59.172 --> 00:04:00.400
scientific
and culture databases.

00:04:00.473 --> 00:04:01.565
Computer chip designs,

00:04:01.641 --> 00:04:03.541
instructions for
building transceivers.

00:04:03.610 --> 00:04:05.202
It's practically
a how-to manual.

00:04:05.278 --> 00:04:08.714
If the Borg had intercepted
this probe,

00:04:08.781 --> 00:04:10.908
humanity would have been
assimilated centuries ago.

00:04:10.984 --> 00:04:13.214
Our ancestors had no
idea what was out here.

00:04:13.286 --> 00:04:16.016
This must have been before
your Prime Directive.

00:04:16.089 --> 00:04:18.216
It was before Starfleet existed.

00:04:18.291 --> 00:04:21.920
In any case, we lost contact
with the probe 130 years ago.

00:04:22.061 --> 00:04:24.120
But its last-known
coordinates...

00:04:24.197 --> 00:04:25.459
Let me guess.

00:04:25.531 --> 00:04:27.795
We're in the neighborhood.

00:04:29.669 --> 00:04:31.899
Starfleet's mapped out
a search grid.

00:04:31.971 --> 00:04:33.939
It'll take us
a little off course,

00:04:34.073 --> 00:04:35.870
but if the probe
is still intact,

00:04:35.942 --> 00:04:37.842
and we're lucky enough
to find it,

00:04:37.910 --> 00:04:40.936
we'll be retrieving
a little piece of history.

00:04:45.752 --> 00:04:50.883
Captain's Log, Stardate 54775.4.

00:04:50.957 --> 00:04:52.948
We've been searching
for five days

00:04:53.026 --> 00:04:54.789
without any sign of the probe,

00:04:54.861 --> 00:04:57.056
but we're not about
to disappoint Starfleet

00:04:57.130 --> 00:04:59.564
on our first official assignment
in seven years.

00:04:59.632 --> 00:05:01.725
Nothing in Grid 295.

00:05:01.801 --> 00:05:03.291
Mr. Paris.

00:05:03.369 --> 00:05:04.893
Moving on.

00:05:04.971 --> 00:05:06.700
We should try
skipping ahead a little

00:05:06.773 --> 00:05:08.570
to Grid 310.

00:05:08.641 --> 00:05:09.767
I stayed up all night

00:05:09.842 --> 00:05:12.003
re-extrapolating
the probe's trajectory.

00:05:12.078 --> 00:05:15.013
I've compensated for
solar winds, ionic interference,

00:05:15.081 --> 00:05:17.515
and a few local anomalies
Starfleet wouldn't

00:05:17.583 --> 00:05:19.813
know about.

00:05:19.886 --> 00:05:21.979
Alter course to Grid 310.

00:05:23.389 --> 00:05:26.324
Trying to impress
the Starfleet brass?

00:05:26.392 --> 00:05:27.723
Just doing my job.

00:05:33.966 --> 00:05:36.161
I'm detecting
a titanium signature

00:05:36.235 --> 00:05:38.601
that matches
the probe's parameters.

00:05:38.671 --> 00:05:39.933
Location?

00:05:40.073 --> 00:05:41.404
A planet two light-years away.

00:05:41.474 --> 00:05:42.941
Confirmed.

00:05:43.009 --> 00:05:44.874
Good job, Harry.

00:05:53.786 --> 00:05:56.619
The readings are coming
from the northern subcontinent.

00:05:56.689 --> 00:05:57.951
Can you localize them?

00:05:58.057 --> 00:05:59.854
There are high levels
of antimatter radiation

00:05:59.926 --> 00:06:02.622
in the atmosphere, scattering
the probe's signature.

00:06:02.695 --> 00:06:03.662
Any life signs?

00:06:04.864 --> 00:06:06.229
None.

00:06:06.299 --> 00:06:07.391
Assemble an away team

00:06:07.467 --> 00:06:09.799
and take the Flyer
down for a closer look.

00:06:14.040 --> 00:06:16.099
You seem to be in a good mood,
Doctor.

00:06:16.175 --> 00:06:17.904
Just excited to be doing my part

00:06:17.977 --> 00:06:20.309
for our first official
mission, Mr. Carey.

00:06:20.380 --> 00:06:24.373
An inoculation a day
keeps the radiation away.

00:06:24.450 --> 00:06:26.884
I took a look at those
atmospheric readings.

00:06:26.953 --> 00:06:28.887
Thermal eddies,
gravimetric shear.

00:06:28.955 --> 00:06:31.048
You're going to need
your best pilot.

00:06:31.124 --> 00:06:32.523
Are you volunteering?

00:06:32.592 --> 00:06:34.150
Well, if the Doc can spare me.

00:06:34.227 --> 00:06:36.627
I'll muddle through.

00:06:38.331 --> 00:06:40.925
If you're here
for your fetal resonance scan,

00:06:41.033 --> 00:06:42.159
you're a day early.

00:06:42.235 --> 00:06:43.668
I'm here for my inoculation.

00:06:43.736 --> 00:06:45.499
You are not going
on this mission.

00:06:45.571 --> 00:06:47.471
Chakotay said he needed
an engineer.

00:06:47.540 --> 00:06:49.132
He's already got one.

00:06:49.208 --> 00:06:50.732
Now he's got two.

00:06:50.810 --> 00:06:53.278
Will you excuse us?

00:06:55.581 --> 00:06:57.071
Any bets on this one?

00:06:57.150 --> 00:06:58.879
My money's on B'Elanna.

00:06:58.951 --> 00:06:59.883
It's been months

00:06:59.952 --> 00:07:01.146
since I've been
on an away mission.

00:07:01.220 --> 00:07:02.881
Then try the holodeck.
The Flyer is full.

00:07:02.955 --> 00:07:04.752
You can make room.

00:07:04.824 --> 00:07:05.882
Neelix doesn't have to go.

00:07:06.025 --> 00:07:07.322
He's not six months pregnant.

00:07:07.393 --> 00:07:09.384
Being pregnant doesn't
make me an invalid.

00:07:11.964 --> 00:07:14.330
No, it doesn't,

00:07:14.400 --> 00:07:16.698
but there's a toxic atmosphere
down there,

00:07:16.769 --> 00:07:18.737
and you're breathing for two.

00:07:23.509 --> 00:07:25.602
All right, you win.

00:07:25.678 --> 00:07:29.546
But if we have another baby,
you carry it,

00:07:29.615 --> 00:07:32.140
and I'll go
on the away missions.

00:07:32.218 --> 00:07:34.345
It's a deal.

00:07:40.593 --> 00:07:42.925
Sorry for the bumpy ride.

00:07:43.062 --> 00:07:45.292
We'll be clearing
the stratosphere

00:07:45.364 --> 00:07:46.592
in about a minute.

00:07:49.936 --> 00:07:52.700
I had a cousin who used
to transport disulfides

00:07:52.772 --> 00:07:54.637
from a gas giant.

00:07:54.707 --> 00:07:56.698
He claimed
to love the turbulence.

00:07:58.244 --> 00:08:02.840
Of course, disulfides
are known to cause delusions.

00:08:02.915 --> 00:08:04.678
Hang on.

00:08:08.321 --> 00:08:09.845
I thought it was uninhabited.

00:08:09.922 --> 00:08:12.356
There's nothing alive
down there now.

00:08:12.425 --> 00:08:15.087
Radiation levels
are at 6,000 isorems.

00:08:15.161 --> 00:08:18.824
I've localized the signature
to a three-kilometer radius.

00:08:18.898 --> 00:08:20.559
Transfer the coordinates
to the helm.

00:08:20.633 --> 00:08:23.534
When we find the probe,
we'll beam it to the cargo hold.

00:08:23.603 --> 00:08:25.400
That may not be easy
with all this radiation.

00:08:25.471 --> 00:08:27.496
We'd better bring
transport enhancers.

00:08:27.573 --> 00:08:29.666
Set us down, Tom.

00:08:29.742 --> 00:08:31.073
Yes, sir.

00:08:31.143 --> 00:08:33.873
Gently, please.

00:08:55.001 --> 00:08:56.832
I should have brought
a holo-camera,

00:08:56.903 --> 00:08:59.838
so I could show B'Elanna
she's not missing anything.

00:08:59.906 --> 00:09:01.373
Can you believe
she actually wanted

00:09:01.440 --> 00:09:03.101
to come with us?

00:09:03.175 --> 00:09:04.699
When my wife was pregnant,

00:09:04.777 --> 00:09:06.870
she didn't want
to be coddled, either.

00:09:08.114 --> 00:09:09.604
And she's not half Klingon.

00:09:09.682 --> 00:09:11.149
Oh, maybe it's us.

00:09:11.217 --> 00:09:12.445
Something about

00:09:12.518 --> 00:09:15.009
fatherhood seems
to regress the male psyche

00:09:15.087 --> 00:09:16.349
a few thousand years.

00:09:31.437 --> 00:09:32.802
Tom, be careful.

00:09:35.274 --> 00:09:36.605
It's a toy.

00:09:38.010 --> 00:09:39.409
Like a music box.

00:09:41.447 --> 00:09:42.914
Vivaldi.

00:09:46.118 --> 00:09:48.382
I'm getting something.

00:09:48.454 --> 00:09:51.514
90 meters this way.

00:09:53.659 --> 00:09:54.819
Souvenir.

00:09:58.831 --> 00:10:03.427
Commander, I'm detecting
an antimatter signature ahead.

00:10:09.108 --> 00:10:11.702
Looks like missile silos.

00:10:11.777 --> 00:10:13.438
Paris to Chakotay.

00:10:13.512 --> 00:10:14.638
Go ahead.

00:10:14.714 --> 00:10:16.705
We've got a reading
that could be the probe.

00:10:16.782 --> 00:10:18.443
It's inside a cave.

00:10:18.517 --> 00:10:20.815
Keep us posted.

00:10:34.133 --> 00:10:36.966
The warhead is still active.

00:10:37.069 --> 00:10:38.536
It wouldn't have taken
many of these

00:10:38.604 --> 00:10:40.572
to trigger a nuclear winter.

00:10:45.978 --> 00:10:48.469
People must have
taken shelter here.

00:10:48.547 --> 00:10:49.980
Well, it makes sense.

00:10:50.049 --> 00:10:51.516
The magnesite in these caves

00:10:51.584 --> 00:10:53.609
would have provided
partial shielding

00:10:53.686 --> 00:10:54.983
from the radiation.

00:10:57.657 --> 00:11:00.148
Over here!

00:11:00.226 --> 00:11:02.057
What'd you find?

00:11:02.128 --> 00:11:05.359
Some kind of control room...
or laboratory.

00:11:05.431 --> 00:11:07.023
Laboratory?

00:11:07.099 --> 00:11:08.828
Lots of diagnostic equipment.

00:11:08.901 --> 00:11:11.062
Looks like it was salvaged
from a junk heap.

00:11:11.137 --> 00:11:13.264
Or scavenged from the ruins.

00:11:21.814 --> 00:11:23.042
Particle scanners,

00:11:23.115 --> 00:11:24.878
circuit analyzers...

00:11:24.950 --> 00:11:26.918
Most of it's still functional.

00:11:31.657 --> 00:11:33.750
They were working on something.

00:11:37.663 --> 00:11:39.824
This is what we came for.

00:11:39.899 --> 00:11:43.426
Whoever lived here
must have been studying it.

00:11:43.502 --> 00:11:46.266
The datacore is still intact.

00:11:46.338 --> 00:11:50.206
Start setting up
the transport enhancers.

00:11:50.276 --> 00:11:51.641
Paris to Chakotay.

00:11:51.711 --> 00:11:52.973
Go ahead.

00:11:53.045 --> 00:11:54.410
We found the probe.

00:11:54.480 --> 00:11:56.471
Well, pieces of it, anyway.

00:11:56.549 --> 00:11:58.915
We're getting ready to beam it
back up to the Flyer.

00:11:58.984 --> 00:12:00.417
We'll meet you there.

00:12:03.522 --> 00:12:05.251
Hello?

00:12:05.324 --> 00:12:06.814
Is someone there?

00:12:06.892 --> 00:12:10.760
The tricorder isn't
reading any life signs.

00:12:48.968 --> 00:12:50.902
Don't move.

00:12:56.308 --> 00:12:58.105
You okay?

00:13:00.813 --> 00:13:03.748
Delta Flyer to Paris.

00:13:03.816 --> 00:13:05.750
Chakotay to away team.
Respond.

00:13:19.498 --> 00:13:21.125
They're antimatter weapons.

00:13:22.835 --> 00:13:24.063
Shields are off-line.

00:13:25.838 --> 00:13:26.930
What are you doing?

00:13:27.039 --> 00:13:28.063
Getting us out of here.

00:13:28.140 --> 00:13:29.402
What about the others?

00:13:29.475 --> 00:13:31.636
We can't do them any good
if we're dead.

00:13:31.710 --> 00:13:33.075
We'll come back for them.

00:13:33.145 --> 00:13:35.045
Look, you're making
a mistake...

00:13:39.585 --> 00:13:42.247
Leave them alone!

00:13:46.525 --> 00:13:47.651
Who are you?

00:13:47.726 --> 00:13:50.126
I'm Lieutenant Tom Paris.

00:13:50.196 --> 00:13:52.494
We're from the Federation
Starship Voyager.

00:13:53.866 --> 00:13:55.026
What are these?

00:13:56.535 --> 00:13:58.935
They're transport enhancers.

00:13:59.004 --> 00:14:01.438
We were going to use them
to retrieve our probe.

00:14:02.474 --> 00:14:04.271
Your probe?

00:14:07.680 --> 00:14:09.875
Too bad you didn't come
for it sooner.

00:14:09.949 --> 00:14:12.440
You would have saved us
a lot of suffering.

00:14:15.855 --> 00:14:17.322
We still can't
contact the others

00:14:17.389 --> 00:14:18.879
or get a fix
on their life signs.

00:14:18.958 --> 00:14:20.425
Why didn't we detect
the aliens?

00:14:20.492 --> 00:14:21.618
I don't know.

00:14:21.694 --> 00:14:24.094
Whoever they are, they
have antimatter weapons.

00:14:24.163 --> 00:14:25.255
Antimatter?

00:14:25.331 --> 00:14:26.662
Bridge to Captain Janeway.

00:14:26.732 --> 00:14:27.858
Go ahead.

00:14:27.933 --> 00:14:29.423
We are being hailed
from the surface.

00:14:29.501 --> 00:14:30.593
The away team?

00:14:30.669 --> 00:14:32.136
No.

00:14:39.511 --> 00:14:41.103
This is Captain Kathryn Janeway.

00:14:41.180 --> 00:14:42.306
Who am I speaking with?

00:14:42.381 --> 00:14:43.939
My name is Verin.

00:14:44.083 --> 00:14:46.950
Your crewmen are my prisoners.

00:14:47.086 --> 00:14:49.418
Why? We haven't done
anything to harm you.

00:14:49.488 --> 00:14:51.080
You committed genocide.

00:14:52.157 --> 00:14:53.749
I think there's been
a misunderstanding.

00:14:53.826 --> 00:14:55.259
We arrived here just...

00:14:55.327 --> 00:14:56.521
You're from Earth?

00:14:56.595 --> 00:14:57.960
Yes.

00:14:58.097 --> 00:15:00.622
Then you're going to pay
for what your people did to us.

00:15:00.699 --> 00:15:03.031
I'm sorry, I don't know
what you're talking about.

00:15:03.102 --> 00:15:04.364
We're not as naive

00:15:04.436 --> 00:15:07.530
as you seem to think
we are, Captain, not anymore.

00:15:10.142 --> 00:15:11.769
What is it you want?

00:15:11.844 --> 00:15:16.577
I want you
to get us off this planet.

00:15:16.649 --> 00:15:19.140
Find us a new home.

00:15:19.218 --> 00:15:22.654
Release my crewmen and
we can talk about it.

00:15:22.721 --> 00:15:24.086
No more talking.

00:15:24.156 --> 00:15:26.886
Your people won't be safe
until mine are.

00:15:26.959 --> 00:15:29.655
Listen, I don't
respond well to threats.

00:15:29.728 --> 00:15:31.787
And I don't want to kill anyone,

00:15:31.864 --> 00:15:34.128
but I will
if you don't cooperate.

00:15:34.199 --> 00:15:35.530
You have three hours

00:15:35.601 --> 00:15:37.125
to begin evacuating us.

00:15:43.542 --> 00:15:45.407
Start scanning
for the nearest M-Class planet.

00:15:45.477 --> 00:15:46.944
You intend to meet his demands?

00:15:47.079 --> 00:15:49.070
I'm just keeping
my options open.

00:15:49.148 --> 00:15:50.115
You're with me.

00:15:53.686 --> 00:15:55.210
I've analyzed his garment.

00:15:55.287 --> 00:15:57.152
It's lined with magnesite.

00:15:57.222 --> 00:15:59.156
A makeshift environmental suit.

00:15:59.224 --> 00:16:01.954
Unfortunately, the protection
it offers is limited.

00:16:02.027 --> 00:16:04.894
His tissues are saturated
with antimatter radiation.

00:16:04.964 --> 00:16:07.728
It explains why we couldn't
detect his life signs.

00:16:07.800 --> 00:16:09.700
They're virtually
indistinguishable

00:16:09.768 --> 00:16:10.996
from the environment.

00:16:11.070 --> 00:16:12.128
Now that we know that,

00:16:12.204 --> 00:16:13.899
maybe we can adjust our
sensors to detect them.

00:16:14.039 --> 00:16:15.165
Let's wake him.

00:16:28.687 --> 00:16:31.622
What were you doing
aboard our shuttle?

00:16:33.392 --> 00:16:35.917
Trying to undo the damage
you caused.

00:16:35.995 --> 00:16:38.555
If you're referring to what's
happened on your planet,

00:16:38.630 --> 00:16:40.222
we had nothing to do with it.

00:16:40.299 --> 00:16:41.789
Your people sent the probe...

00:16:43.168 --> 00:16:44.328
...didn't they?

00:16:44.403 --> 00:16:46.667
Our ancestors sent it
300 years ago,

00:16:46.739 --> 00:16:49.037
to make contact
with other species.

00:16:49.108 --> 00:16:50.973
They did
a little more than that.

00:16:52.611 --> 00:16:53.703
Am I your prisoner?

00:16:53.779 --> 00:16:55.144
No. You're suffering

00:16:55.214 --> 00:16:57.546
from prolonged
radiation exposure.

00:16:57.616 --> 00:16:58.708
I can treat you.

00:16:58.784 --> 00:17:00.342
You can?

00:17:00.419 --> 00:17:01.886
I believe I can.

00:17:03.188 --> 00:17:05.520
In exchange for what?

00:17:05.591 --> 00:17:07.388
Nothing.

00:17:09.395 --> 00:17:12.762
I have a wife, friends.

00:17:12.831 --> 00:17:15.766
We might be able
to help them, too,

00:17:15.834 --> 00:17:19.065
but not while our crewmen
are being held hostage.

00:17:19.138 --> 00:17:22.596
You said you were trying
to undo the damage we caused.

00:17:22.674 --> 00:17:24.642
What did you mean by that?

00:17:25.677 --> 00:17:26.905
I was aboard your shuttle

00:17:26.979 --> 00:17:28.503
looking for technology

00:17:28.580 --> 00:17:31.674
that might help us
neutralize the radiation.

00:17:31.750 --> 00:17:33.615
We saw missiles on the surface.

00:17:33.685 --> 00:17:35.778
Was the destruction
caused by war?

00:17:35.854 --> 00:17:37.651
Those missiles were built
for defense.

00:17:37.723 --> 00:17:38.917
They were never launched.

00:17:38.991 --> 00:17:40.618
Then what accounts
for the devastation?

00:17:40.692 --> 00:17:44.719
A containment failure
in our power grid.

00:17:44.797 --> 00:17:46.628
Once the antimatter
was released,

00:17:46.698 --> 00:17:48.063
it destroyed everything.

00:17:48.133 --> 00:17:52.433
I'm sorry, but I still don't see
how we're responsible.

00:17:52.504 --> 00:17:55.735
Before the probe,

00:17:55.808 --> 00:17:59.938
my people never conceived
of anything like antimatter.

00:18:00.045 --> 00:18:03.310
"We offer this information
freely with the hope

00:18:03.382 --> 00:18:05.873
"that one day
we will stand on your soil

00:18:05.984 --> 00:18:08.544
and extend our hands
in friendship."

00:18:08.620 --> 00:18:10.747
I'm sure you recognize
those words.

00:18:10.823 --> 00:18:12.723
The recording from the probe.

00:18:12.791 --> 00:18:17.057
Your people sent us technology
that they knew would destroy us.

00:18:17.129 --> 00:18:19.097
I don't understand.

00:18:19.164 --> 00:18:21.029
We didn't either at first,

00:18:21.100 --> 00:18:22.761
but we had decades
to think about it,

00:18:22.835 --> 00:18:25.736
and now it seems so obvious.

00:18:25.804 --> 00:18:29.365
You send us new technology,
encourage us to use it,

00:18:29.441 --> 00:18:32.899
and then you wait for us
to obliterate ourselves.

00:18:33.011 --> 00:18:34.569
Why would we do that?

00:18:34.646 --> 00:18:36.113
Because it's easier
than invading us.

00:18:36.181 --> 00:18:39.446
Do you really believe
we'd contaminate a world

00:18:39.518 --> 00:18:41.179
we intended to conquer?

00:18:41.253 --> 00:18:43.221
I'm a scientist.

00:18:43.288 --> 00:18:45.654
I believe what I see.

00:18:45.724 --> 00:18:48.284
And today, I saw your people
standing on our soil

00:18:48.360 --> 00:18:49.486
just as you promised,

00:18:49.561 --> 00:18:51.756
and they were wearing
equipment that protected them

00:18:51.830 --> 00:18:53.923
from the radiation,
because they knew

00:18:53.999 --> 00:18:57.662
exactly what to expect.

00:18:57.736 --> 00:19:02.639
If you were in my position,
what would you believe?

00:19:10.048 --> 00:19:11.879
He might have a concussion.

00:19:11.984 --> 00:19:14.282
I need the medkit from my pack.

00:19:14.353 --> 00:19:17.481
I was told not
to let you use your equipment.

00:19:23.695 --> 00:19:25.856
When's your baby due?

00:19:29.735 --> 00:19:31.635
My wife's pregnant, too.

00:19:31.703 --> 00:19:34.638
We're expecting a little girl
in a couple of months.

00:19:34.706 --> 00:19:36.674
How do you know it's a girl?

00:19:36.742 --> 00:19:38.175
Well, we have technology

00:19:38.243 --> 00:19:41.144
that allows us
to examine the fetus.

00:19:41.213 --> 00:19:42.339
She has my eyes

00:19:42.414 --> 00:19:44.245
and her mother's cranial ridges.

00:19:48.487 --> 00:19:50.079
Is this your first?

00:19:52.224 --> 00:19:53.816
No.

00:19:53.892 --> 00:19:55.189
Oh.

00:19:55.260 --> 00:19:57.228
Boys? Girls?

00:19:58.297 --> 00:20:00.891
Two boys and a girl.

00:20:02.534 --> 00:20:04.001
What are their names?

00:20:07.372 --> 00:20:09.203
They were all stillborn.

00:20:12.644 --> 00:20:14.441
I'm sorry.

00:20:14.513 --> 00:20:18.279
You're... a doctor?

00:20:18.350 --> 00:20:20.477
No, I'm just a medic.

00:20:22.588 --> 00:20:25.580
But we have the best doctor
in the Quadrant back on Voyager.

00:20:25.657 --> 00:20:27.454
He might be able to help...

00:20:27.526 --> 00:20:29.619
I shouldn't be talking to you.

00:20:33.198 --> 00:20:37.794
Our current coordinates
and the nearest M-Class planet...

00:20:37.869 --> 00:20:39.461
132 light-years away.

00:20:39.538 --> 00:20:40.766
At maximum warp,

00:20:40.839 --> 00:20:42.864
that's about two months
round trip.

00:20:42.941 --> 00:20:45.102
How many people are
we talking about?

00:20:45.177 --> 00:20:47.168
If these sensor modifications
are correct,

00:20:47.246 --> 00:20:49.908
about 5,500.

00:20:49.982 --> 00:20:51.973
It would take
at least 17 trips...

00:20:52.050 --> 00:20:54.917
almost three years...
to complete the relocation.

00:20:54.987 --> 00:20:56.784
We've made sacrifices
to help people before.

00:20:56.855 --> 00:20:58.516
What about Tom and the others?

00:20:58.590 --> 00:21:00.114
Are they supposed
to rot down there

00:21:00.192 --> 00:21:01.659
until this relocation's
finished?

00:21:01.727 --> 00:21:03.695
I don't think
Verin's going to let go

00:21:03.762 --> 00:21:05.320
of his only bargaining chips.

00:21:05.397 --> 00:21:08.127
Then we may have to use force.

00:21:08.200 --> 00:21:11.226
Not until we've exhausted
every other option.

00:21:11.303 --> 00:21:14.272
These people believe
that we're violent.

00:21:14.339 --> 00:21:17.672
I'm not going to do anything
to reinforce that belief,

00:21:17.743 --> 00:21:22.146
unless it becomes
absolutely necessary.

00:21:28.987 --> 00:21:30.750
I've extracted the nanoprobes.

00:21:30.822 --> 00:21:32.653
I'll begin reprogramming them.

00:21:34.760 --> 00:21:36.819
Nanoprobes?

00:21:36.895 --> 00:21:38.226
Microscopic machines.

00:21:38.297 --> 00:21:41.698
Hopefully they'll help us
repair your damaged tissue.

00:21:41.767 --> 00:21:44.167
You said you extracted them.

00:21:44.236 --> 00:21:45.726
From where?

00:21:45.804 --> 00:21:46.964
My bloodstream.

00:21:47.105 --> 00:21:49.335
They maintain
my cybernetic implants.

00:21:49.408 --> 00:21:52.969
Nanoprobes, cybernetic implants.

00:21:53.045 --> 00:21:56.310
Are others
on your crew like you?

00:21:56.381 --> 00:21:59.782
No, I'm... unique.

00:21:59.851 --> 00:22:01.682
You certainly are.

00:22:01.753 --> 00:22:04.586
I need a word with your patient.

00:22:05.657 --> 00:22:07.648
You told me you've been
looking for ways

00:22:07.726 --> 00:22:09.159
to neutralize the radiation.

00:22:09.227 --> 00:22:11.559
All my life.

00:22:11.630 --> 00:22:14.394
Tell me about your work.

00:22:19.738 --> 00:22:21.501
Lieutenant?

00:22:21.573 --> 00:22:22.835
I'm okay.

00:22:22.908 --> 00:22:24.808
My stomach's
just a little queasy.

00:22:24.876 --> 00:22:27.140
Our inoculations
must be wearing off.

00:22:27.212 --> 00:22:29.407
I thought these caves
were naturally shielded.

00:22:29.481 --> 00:22:32.473
They're no substitute
for an environmental suit.

00:22:32.551 --> 00:22:34.212
These people have lived here
all their lives

00:22:34.286 --> 00:22:35.480
without environmental suits.

00:22:35.554 --> 00:22:37.886
These people have lived here
without much of anything.

00:22:39.758 --> 00:22:43.216
- Hello.
- Hello.

00:22:43.295 --> 00:22:45.957
It's all right.
We're not going to hurt you.

00:22:46.098 --> 00:22:47.690
What's your name?

00:22:48.767 --> 00:22:50.064
Yun.

00:22:50.135 --> 00:22:51.966
Uh, mine's Tom.

00:22:52.070 --> 00:22:53.901
This is Joe and Neelix.

00:22:59.578 --> 00:23:01.910
You're not like them.

00:23:01.980 --> 00:23:06.610
We're different species,
but they're my friends.

00:23:08.620 --> 00:23:10.349
They say you're going
to take us on your ship

00:23:10.422 --> 00:23:12.856
and find us a new home.

00:23:12.924 --> 00:23:16.052
I'm sure our Captain
is trying to help you.

00:23:16.128 --> 00:23:20.258
Neelix...
where's our "souvenir"?

00:23:21.600 --> 00:23:23.864
In my pack.

00:23:23.935 --> 00:23:26.267
Uh, excuse me.

00:23:26.338 --> 00:23:29.603
Um, we'd like
to give her something.

00:23:29.674 --> 00:23:32.336
It's in the equipment bag.

00:23:33.011 --> 00:23:35.377
It's a toy.

00:24:00.972 --> 00:24:03.463
That could be a weapon.

00:24:07.479 --> 00:24:08.639
It's harmless.

00:24:14.753 --> 00:24:17.347
These men are dangerous.

00:24:17.422 --> 00:24:19.185
I want you to stay away
from them.

00:24:19.257 --> 00:24:20.884
Understood?

00:24:27.599 --> 00:24:30.591
Well, so much
for making friends.

00:24:31.837 --> 00:24:32.929
Mr. Verin?

00:24:33.004 --> 00:24:34.164
What are you doing?

00:24:34.239 --> 00:24:35.706
My job.

00:24:35.774 --> 00:24:38.265
I'm Voyager's Ambassador,
remember?

00:24:38.343 --> 00:24:41.779
Can I have a word with you?

00:24:55.393 --> 00:24:57.384
Just between us...

00:24:58.697 --> 00:25:00.961
I understand why you
don't trust humans.

00:25:01.066 --> 00:25:03.830
Then why are you with them?

00:25:03.902 --> 00:25:07.998
They're not so bad once
you get to know them.

00:25:08.073 --> 00:25:10.007
When I first met them,

00:25:10.075 --> 00:25:13.340
I thought they were arrogant,
self-righteous.

00:25:13.411 --> 00:25:15.003
I suppose
you're going to tell me

00:25:15.080 --> 00:25:16.342
you've changed your mind.

00:25:16.414 --> 00:25:18.507
Well, not completely.

00:25:18.583 --> 00:25:21.177
I still think
they take themselves

00:25:21.253 --> 00:25:23.551
far too seriously
for my taste...

00:25:25.490 --> 00:25:29.324
but one thing they don't do
is harm other people.

00:25:29.394 --> 00:25:30.861
Are you blind?

00:25:30.929 --> 00:25:35.263
No, I see very clearly
what's happened to you,

00:25:35.333 --> 00:25:36.766
and I'd like to help.

00:25:37.836 --> 00:25:39.133
How?

00:25:39.204 --> 00:25:41.502
My Captain listens to me.

00:25:41.573 --> 00:25:43.370
I can speak to her
on your behalf,

00:25:43.441 --> 00:25:45.238
help her understand
your situation.

00:25:45.310 --> 00:25:49.007
What do you know
about our "situation"?

00:25:51.449 --> 00:25:53.940
I know what
you've been through.

00:25:54.019 --> 00:25:57.352
My planet was destroyed
by a weapon

00:25:57.422 --> 00:25:59.322
called a metreon cascade.

00:25:59.391 --> 00:26:03.555
Hundreds of thousands
of people were killed...

00:26:03.628 --> 00:26:05.858
including my family.

00:26:06.932 --> 00:26:08.763
How did you survive?

00:26:08.833 --> 00:26:13.736
I was on a neighboring planet
when the weapon was detonated.

00:26:13.805 --> 00:26:18.902
I went back with a rescue team,
but there was no one left.

00:26:18.977 --> 00:26:21.707
I'm sorry about what happened
to your family...

00:26:23.815 --> 00:26:25.783
but don't compare your life
to mine.

00:26:34.225 --> 00:26:36.921
The nearest suitable planet
is simply too far away,

00:26:36.995 --> 00:26:39.930
so I'd like to propose
an alternative.

00:26:40.031 --> 00:26:41.191
There is no alternative.

00:26:41.266 --> 00:26:42.358
Please, hear me out.

00:26:42.434 --> 00:26:45.597
We have one of your people
aboard, a Mr. Otrin.

00:26:45.670 --> 00:26:47.900
He has some interesting ideas

00:26:47.973 --> 00:26:50.373
about counteracting
the radiation.

00:26:50.442 --> 00:26:54.242
Otrin has too many ideas.

00:26:54.312 --> 00:26:57.076
I think his theories have merit.

00:26:57.148 --> 00:27:01.642
What he's lacked until now
is the means to carry them out.

00:27:01.720 --> 00:27:04.518
If you release the hostages,
we can work together.

00:27:04.589 --> 00:27:06.181
There's a good chance

00:27:06.257 --> 00:27:09.420
we could undo some of the damage
to your environment.

00:27:09.494 --> 00:27:11.052
This isn't a negotiation.

00:27:11.129 --> 00:27:12.994
You don't seem to understand.

00:27:13.064 --> 00:27:15.828
It would take years to evacuate
the entire planet.

00:27:15.900 --> 00:27:18.266
So instead,
you once again offer us

00:27:18.336 --> 00:27:20.896
the benefits of your technology.

00:27:21.006 --> 00:27:24.874
What I'm offering you
is a realistic alternative.

00:27:24.943 --> 00:27:28.071
If I release the hostages,

00:27:28.146 --> 00:27:32.173
what's to prevent you
from leaving or attacking us?

00:27:32.250 --> 00:27:35.014
Look, I know you've suffered,
and I know you don't trust us.

00:27:35.086 --> 00:27:37.281
You haven't given me
any reason to.

00:27:37.355 --> 00:27:40.722
Then why don't we start
with a small step?

00:27:40.792 --> 00:27:43.420
You return one of the hostages,

00:27:43.495 --> 00:27:47.295
and I'll send you a supply
of food and medicine.

00:28:01.379 --> 00:28:05.315
You... what's your name?

00:28:05.383 --> 00:28:07.146
Joe Carey.

00:28:07.218 --> 00:28:11.814
Set up your...
transport enhancers.

00:28:38.616 --> 00:28:42.313
I'm sorry... Mr. Carey.

00:28:45.757 --> 00:28:46.883
Sorry?

00:28:46.958 --> 00:28:50.291
Your crewman's ready, Captain.

00:28:50.361 --> 00:28:52.420
Transport him to Sick Bay.

00:28:54.699 --> 00:28:57.099
Hey, what the hell
are you doing?!

00:28:57.168 --> 00:28:59.261
Tom?

00:28:59.337 --> 00:29:01.703
Sick Bay to Bridge.

00:29:02.941 --> 00:29:05.239
They've killed Lieutenant Carey.

00:29:14.953 --> 00:29:16.750
If you think murdering
one of my crewmen

00:29:16.821 --> 00:29:19.153
is going to make me
more receptive to your demands,

00:29:19.224 --> 00:29:20.486
you're mistaken.

00:29:20.558 --> 00:29:24.289
Don't force me
to kill anyone else.

00:29:27.732 --> 00:29:31.896
All right.
I'll evacuate your people,

00:29:32.003 --> 00:29:34.301
but our transporters
aren't designed

00:29:34.372 --> 00:29:36.169
to accommodate large groups.

00:29:36.241 --> 00:29:39.176
We'll need time to modify them.

00:29:39.244 --> 00:29:42.145
We'll be ready within the hour.

00:29:42.213 --> 00:29:43.805
If you're not...

00:29:43.882 --> 00:29:47.045
I understand.

00:29:47.118 --> 00:29:48.210
My ready room.

00:29:49.621 --> 00:29:51.316
You have radiation poisoning.

00:29:51.389 --> 00:29:53.220
This will make you feel better.

00:29:53.291 --> 00:29:55.316
Thank you.

00:29:55.393 --> 00:29:58.920
Why are you helping us?

00:29:58.997 --> 00:30:02.262
Your child's going
to need a father...

00:30:03.668 --> 00:30:04.760
isn't she?

00:30:10.441 --> 00:30:13.604
The first phase
of your therapy is complete.

00:30:15.246 --> 00:30:18.044
How do you feel?

00:30:18.116 --> 00:30:19.378
I can breathe more easily.

00:30:19.450 --> 00:30:21.179
Your lungs were damaged
by the radiation.

00:30:21.252 --> 00:30:24.813
The nanoprobes
are repairing them.

00:30:24.889 --> 00:30:27.790
It's incredible.

00:30:27.859 --> 00:30:30.794
If we could manufacture
more of these,

00:30:30.862 --> 00:30:33.660
we might be able
to treat everyone.

00:30:33.731 --> 00:30:37.360
Unfortunately, Mr. Verin
has refused our help.

00:30:37.435 --> 00:30:39.926
Did you expect him to cooperate?

00:30:40.004 --> 00:30:42.973
His behavior is irrational.

00:30:43.107 --> 00:30:44.199
To you, maybe,

00:30:44.275 --> 00:30:47.301
but you haven't
lived like we have.

00:30:47.378 --> 00:30:49.141
No, but that doesn't mean

00:30:49.214 --> 00:30:51.614
that we're responsible
for what's happened here.

00:30:51.683 --> 00:30:53.548
You can't deny
your people sent the probe.

00:30:53.618 --> 00:30:56.519
They made
an error in judgment.

00:30:56.588 --> 00:30:57.987
They failed to anticipate

00:30:58.122 --> 00:30:59.987
the consequences
of their actions,

00:31:00.091 --> 00:31:02.150
but they never meant
to destroy your world.

00:31:02.227 --> 00:31:05.663
Human culture has evolved,
learned from its mistakes.

00:31:05.730 --> 00:31:07.755
So can yours.

00:31:09.667 --> 00:31:16.197
Even if I believed you,
Verin never would.

00:31:16.274 --> 00:31:19.107
Then your people may need
a change of leadership,

00:31:19.177 --> 00:31:22.943
someone more open to new ideas.

00:31:23.047 --> 00:31:24.912
I'm not a leader.

00:31:24.983 --> 00:31:26.780
But you're a scientist,

00:31:26.851 --> 00:31:30.685
someone who can see a problem
and envision a solution.

00:31:30.755 --> 00:31:33.087
The same definition
could apply to a leader.

00:31:36.394 --> 00:31:39.158
Doesn't seem fair, does it?

00:31:39.230 --> 00:31:41.926
My daughter...
she'll have food,

00:31:42.000 --> 00:31:44.969
medical care,
everything she needs.

00:31:46.404 --> 00:31:47.837
What's wrong?

00:31:47.906 --> 00:31:50.374
We need help.

00:31:50.441 --> 00:31:52.966
It's the baby.

00:31:53.044 --> 00:31:56.502
It's too soon.

00:31:58.116 --> 00:32:00.880
Let him help me.

00:32:04.789 --> 00:32:06.051
Can you?

00:32:06.124 --> 00:32:11.289
I think so,
but I'll need my medkit.

00:32:19.971 --> 00:32:21.734
Inform Verin.

00:32:27.045 --> 00:32:28.478
I'm losing the heartbeat.

00:32:28.546 --> 00:32:29.376
Oh, no!

00:32:29.447 --> 00:32:30.379
What are you doing?

00:32:30.448 --> 00:32:31.574
Speeding up the contractions.

00:32:36.688 --> 00:32:38.315
Their ship's returned.

00:32:43.728 --> 00:32:45.218
Send out patrols.

00:32:45.296 --> 00:32:47.594
Double the guard
at the entrance.

00:33:11.489 --> 00:33:14.219
I've got him!

00:33:14.292 --> 00:33:16.920
He's not breathing.

00:33:16.995 --> 00:33:18.587
Cardio-stimulator.

00:33:21.232 --> 00:33:23.132
Three millijoules.

00:33:25.703 --> 00:33:27.102
Now.

00:33:32.176 --> 00:33:34.144
Don't move.

00:33:37.181 --> 00:33:39.445
I'll take him to Verin.

00:33:39.517 --> 00:33:41.417
Find the others.

00:33:43.521 --> 00:33:45.512
This way. Move!

00:33:49.127 --> 00:33:51.322
Increase the charge
to five millijoules.

00:33:53.898 --> 00:33:55.160
Again.

00:33:57.969 --> 00:34:00.062
I'm reading a heartbeat.

00:34:06.077 --> 00:34:07.408
Oh!

00:34:12.650 --> 00:34:14.948
You have a son.

00:34:16.988 --> 00:34:18.683
Oh.

00:34:20.358 --> 00:34:22.485
One of the patrols
took another prisoner.

00:34:24.762 --> 00:34:26.627
Put him with the others.

00:34:35.706 --> 00:34:38.266
We need to get him to Voyager.

00:34:38.342 --> 00:34:40.003
He stays here.

00:34:41.779 --> 00:34:43.178
Mr. Tuvok?

00:34:45.283 --> 00:34:48.377
Your Captain was foolish enough
to think she could rescue you.

00:34:48.453 --> 00:34:51.149
Instead, she's given me
another hostage.

00:35:01.032 --> 00:35:02.522
Doc?

00:35:02.600 --> 00:35:05.125
When you need to infiltrate
a toxic environment,

00:35:05.203 --> 00:35:06.795
it helps to be a hologram.

00:35:06.871 --> 00:35:08.736
Prepare the transport enhancers.

00:35:08.806 --> 00:35:09.864
Tuvok to Chakotay.

00:35:09.941 --> 00:35:11.374
We've secured the hostages.

00:35:11.442 --> 00:35:13.569
Good work.

00:35:14.612 --> 00:35:16.239
Chakotay to Delta Flyer.

00:35:16.314 --> 00:35:18.077
Two to beam out.

00:35:25.723 --> 00:35:27.190
Thank you.

00:35:29.227 --> 00:35:31.058
Now, Mr. Paris.

00:35:34.799 --> 00:35:38.701
Your baby won't survive
without treatment.

00:35:38.769 --> 00:35:41.533
I promise we'll bring him back.

00:35:50.581 --> 00:35:52.742
Take good care of him.

00:35:52.817 --> 00:35:54.375
I will.

00:36:05.696 --> 00:36:08.790
Tuvok to Voyager.

00:36:08.866 --> 00:36:11.835
Five to beam up.

00:36:22.079 --> 00:36:24.172
Cute little fellow, isn't he?

00:36:24.248 --> 00:36:26.273
He's already
responding to treatment.

00:36:26.350 --> 00:36:27.476
Once he's stabilized,

00:36:27.552 --> 00:36:29.349
we'll transport him
to the surface,

00:36:29.420 --> 00:36:31.911
and send along some food
and medical supplies.

00:36:32.056 --> 00:36:33.887
We're leaving?

00:36:33.958 --> 00:36:36.222
As soon as I report
to Starfleet.

00:36:41.132 --> 00:36:42.565
Captain.

00:36:42.633 --> 00:36:44.430
Once the baby's back
in that environment,

00:36:44.502 --> 00:36:46.026
he's just going
to get sick again.

00:36:46.103 --> 00:36:48.162
I'm sorry, we can't keep
him from his mother.

00:36:48.239 --> 00:36:49.866
I'm not suggesting that.

00:36:49.941 --> 00:36:51.408
You told those people

00:36:51.475 --> 00:36:53.636
that we might be able to
neutralize the radiation.

00:36:53.711 --> 00:36:54.803
Was that true?

00:36:54.879 --> 00:36:56.312
Yes, but they didn't
want our help.

00:36:56.380 --> 00:36:57.506
I can't force it on them.

00:36:57.582 --> 00:36:58.844
Maybe you should.

00:36:58.916 --> 00:37:01.180
If we help them without
asking anything in return,

00:37:01.252 --> 00:37:02.879
it'll prove
they're wrong about us.

00:37:02.954 --> 00:37:04.319
You're forgetting something.

00:37:04.388 --> 00:37:05.616
They killed Mr. Carey.

00:37:05.690 --> 00:37:07.214
I'm not about to risk
any more lives

00:37:07.291 --> 00:37:08.258
to help murderers.

00:37:08.326 --> 00:37:10.419
Captain, it was one man
who killed Carey.

00:37:10.494 --> 00:37:14.760
If you saw how they were living,
how desperate they are...

00:37:14.832 --> 00:37:16.766
I'm not saying we should
ignore what happened,

00:37:16.834 --> 00:37:18.529
but humans did play a part
in their suffering.

00:37:18.603 --> 00:37:20.298
Intentional or not,

00:37:20.371 --> 00:37:22.999
that probe had a terrible
impact on these people.

00:37:23.074 --> 00:37:25.133
If there's anything we can
do to make up for that now,

00:37:25.209 --> 00:37:26.733
we at least have to try.

00:37:29.347 --> 00:37:31.042
I've adjusted
the radiation levels

00:37:31.115 --> 00:37:33.345
to match the conditions
on the surface.

00:37:33.417 --> 00:37:35.908
Watch.

00:37:35.987 --> 00:37:37.352
An isolytic chain reaction.

00:37:37.421 --> 00:37:39.685
It recombines
the nucleonic particles

00:37:39.757 --> 00:37:41.748
in the atmosphere.

00:37:45.830 --> 00:37:48.856
How do we apply your methods
on a planetary scale?

00:37:48.933 --> 00:37:51.629
Atmospheric processors
are one possibility.

00:37:51.702 --> 00:37:54.865
Too bad we don't have a corps
of engineers to build them.

00:37:57.208 --> 00:37:59.073
What if we encased
the catalytic agent

00:37:59.143 --> 00:38:00.269
in photon torpedoes,

00:38:00.344 --> 00:38:02.710
used the concussive force
to start the reaction?

00:38:03.948 --> 00:38:05.040
It would require

00:38:05.116 --> 00:38:07.880
multiple detonations
at a low altitude,

00:38:07.952 --> 00:38:10.011
but I believe it could work.

00:38:10.087 --> 00:38:12.885
Captain, an isolitic reaction
of that magnitude

00:38:12.957 --> 00:38:14.754
would expand exponentially.

00:38:14.825 --> 00:38:16.725
Your ship might not survive.

00:38:16.794 --> 00:38:18.728
We'll have to modify
our shields,

00:38:18.796 --> 00:38:20.627
reinforce structural integrity.

00:38:20.698 --> 00:38:22.723
Well, let's get started.

00:38:25.136 --> 00:38:27.400
He's beautiful.

00:38:27.471 --> 00:38:30.804
And they can give us enough
medicine to treat everyone.

00:38:30.875 --> 00:38:32.809
Can they rebuild our cities?

00:38:32.877 --> 00:38:34.902
Bring back the people who died?

00:38:35.046 --> 00:38:36.638
They're offering to help,

00:38:36.714 --> 00:38:38.909
and this time
no one's coercing them.

00:38:38.983 --> 00:38:41.042
We can't trust these people.

00:38:41.118 --> 00:38:43.586
They just sent armed men
to attack us.

00:38:43.654 --> 00:38:45.144
They only wanted
to rescue their hostages.

00:38:45.222 --> 00:38:47.486
Who knows what they wanted?

00:38:47.558 --> 00:38:49.423
You're being irrational.

00:38:49.493 --> 00:38:53.020
What's irrational
is cooperating with the enemy.

00:38:53.097 --> 00:38:55.463
Look at my child.

00:38:55.533 --> 00:38:58.934
They said
that they would treat him,

00:38:59.036 --> 00:39:01.834
and they kept their word.

00:39:04.975 --> 00:39:07.705
Shield modifications on line.

00:39:07.778 --> 00:39:09.746
Torpedoes?

00:39:09.814 --> 00:39:10.974
Ready.

00:39:11.048 --> 00:39:12.310
Hail them.

00:39:14.785 --> 00:39:15.877
Listen to me.

00:39:15.953 --> 00:39:18.751
Otrin, we're ready to begin.

00:39:18.823 --> 00:39:21.587
Understood.

00:39:23.094 --> 00:39:25.460
Good luck.

00:39:25.529 --> 00:39:26.860
Tom, take us down.

00:39:36.307 --> 00:39:39.003
We're 10,000 meters
into the troposphere.

00:39:39.076 --> 00:39:40.976
Fire the first sequence.

00:39:54.024 --> 00:39:55.491
They're attacking us!

00:39:55.559 --> 00:39:57.424
It's only the shock wave
from the detonations.

00:39:58.662 --> 00:40:00.129
No.

00:40:03.768 --> 00:40:05.133
Shields?

00:40:05.202 --> 00:40:06.794
Holding at 18 percent.

00:40:08.806 --> 00:40:12.105
Are you going to stand there
while he helps them destroy us?

00:40:17.381 --> 00:40:18.780
What are you doing?

00:40:19.817 --> 00:40:21.341
Fighting back.

00:40:26.257 --> 00:40:27.952
Captain, they're opening
missile silos.

00:40:28.092 --> 00:40:29.354
They're targeting Voyager.

00:40:29.427 --> 00:40:31.156
At 18 percent, our
shields won't withstand

00:40:31.228 --> 00:40:32.923
an antimatter explosion.

00:40:32.997 --> 00:40:34.589
We should return to orbit.

00:40:34.665 --> 00:40:35.927
Not yet.

00:40:36.000 --> 00:40:37.467
Fire the next sequence.

00:40:39.737 --> 00:40:41.261
You can't launch those missiles!

00:40:41.338 --> 00:40:42.600
Hold him!

00:40:42.673 --> 00:40:44.334
Stop!

00:40:46.076 --> 00:40:47.703
What are you doing?

00:40:47.778 --> 00:40:50.178
I won't let you ruin our
only chance for survival.

00:40:51.682 --> 00:40:53.547
You'd kill me?

00:40:55.352 --> 00:40:56.842
To save my child...

00:40:56.921 --> 00:40:58.855
yes.

00:40:58.923 --> 00:41:01.585
Get that weapon away from her.

00:41:01.659 --> 00:41:04.423
No... sir.

00:41:04.495 --> 00:41:06.929
I've kept you alive...

00:41:07.031 --> 00:41:08.362
all of you!

00:41:08.432 --> 00:41:10.832
And we're grateful for that.

00:41:10.901 --> 00:41:13.870
But survival
isn't enough anymore.

00:41:13.938 --> 00:41:16.873
Are you in command now?

00:41:18.776 --> 00:41:20.368
If I have to be.

00:41:21.779 --> 00:41:23.576
Everyone,

00:41:23.647 --> 00:41:24.739
come outside! Hurry!

00:41:24.815 --> 00:41:25.839
All right, come on.

00:41:25.916 --> 00:41:26.940
What's going on?

00:41:27.051 --> 00:41:28.143
Bring him.

00:41:28.219 --> 00:41:29.345
This way.

00:41:43.868 --> 00:41:45.335
It's beautiful.

00:41:53.344 --> 00:41:55.403
Captain's Log, supplemental.

00:41:55.479 --> 00:41:57.970
We've retrieved Friendship I

00:41:58.082 --> 00:42:00.243
and resumed our course
to the Alpha Quadrant,

00:42:00.317 --> 00:42:04.117
but the success of our mission
had a very high price.

00:42:07.791 --> 00:42:09.725
Impressive, isn't it?

00:42:09.793 --> 00:42:12.591
The detail's amazing.

00:42:14.198 --> 00:42:15.859
Carey spent months
working on it.

00:42:15.933 --> 00:42:18.163
He used to joke
that it wouldn't be finished

00:42:18.235 --> 00:42:19.930
by the time
we got back to Earth.

00:42:20.004 --> 00:42:23.235
He only had one nacelle to go.

00:42:25.376 --> 00:42:28.868
We were able to download
the probe's memory core.

00:42:28.946 --> 00:42:32.814
We'll transmit the telemetry
in the next datastream.

00:42:34.184 --> 00:42:36.277
I think about our ancestors...

00:42:36.353 --> 00:42:37.786
thousands of years

00:42:37.855 --> 00:42:40.722
wondering if they were alone
in the universe,

00:42:40.791 --> 00:42:42.952
finally discovering
they weren't.

00:42:43.027 --> 00:42:46.463
You can't blame them
for wanting to reach out,

00:42:46.530 --> 00:42:49.624
see how many other species
were out there

00:42:49.700 --> 00:42:51.725
asking the same questions.

00:42:51.802 --> 00:42:54.270
The urge to explore
is pretty powerful.

00:42:54.338 --> 00:42:58.240
But it can't justify
the loss of lives...

00:42:58.309 --> 00:43:00.709
whether it's millions...

00:43:02.046 --> 00:43:04.674
or just one.
